# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#      GOOGLE APPLICATION CREDENTIALS - CONFIGURATION
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# To authenticate with your Google Cloud project, you can use either of the
# two methods below. Method 1 is recommended.
#
# After configuring, rename this file from `.env.example` to `.env`
# The application will load it automatically.
#
# IMPORTANT: Add `.env` to your `.gitignore` file to keep secrets safe!

# --- METHOD 1: Service Account File (Recommended) ---
# 1. Download the JSON key file for a service account from your GCP project.
# 2. Paste the FULL path to the file below.
# 3. Uncomment the line.

# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS="C:\Users\YourName\Downloads\your-project-credentials.json"


# --- METHOD 2: gcloud CLI Login (Alternative for local dev) ---
# If you prefer not to use a service account file, you can authenticate via the CLI.
# 1. Make sure the line above is commented out.
# 2. Run the following command in your terminal:
#    gcloud auth application-default login
# 3. Your browser will open for you to log in with your Google account.
# 4. The application will automatically find these credentials.
